{"id":280489619954137,"type":"album","name":"Abattoir Blues / The Lyre of Orpheus","artist":"Nick Cave & the Bad Seeds","year":2004,"weight":19,"info":{"cover":"https://dn721206.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-9c672e25-d735-4fc8-a258-afe81640086a/mbid-9c672e25-d735-4fc8-a258-afe81640086a-42531538540.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":9,"country":"XE","yt":"2bYtFBJajI0","desc":"The album was produced by Nick Launay at Studio Ferber in Paris in March–April 2004 and Nick Cave used The Bad Seeds line up of Mick Harvey, Thomas Wydler, Martyn Casey, Conway Savage, Jim Sclavunos, Warren Ellis, and James Johnston. It was the first album by the group for which Blixa Bargeld did not perform – English guitarist and organist Johnston, of the group Gallon Drunk, replaced Bargeld. Cave decided to split drumming duties for the two parts, with Sclavunos on Abattoir Blues and Wydler on The Lyre of Orpheus. According to Launay, the whole album was completed in twelve .","sputnik":4.06,"links":{"sputnikmusic":"https://www.sputnikmusic.com/album/8952/Nick-Cave-and-The-Bad-Seeds-Abattoir-Blues-The-Lyre-Of-Orpheus/"}},"artist_ref":{"id":96262522505973,"name":"Nick Cave & the Bad Seeds","info":{"img":null}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":185670346256268,"type":"genre","name":"rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":3782,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":210192360016800,"type":"genre","name":"Alternative Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":2664,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":31482837869539,"type":"genre","name":"Punk","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":2333,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":8412226417108,"type":"genre","name":"Indie Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1139,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":163225726165579,"type":"genre","name":"Blues Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":458,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":93579530230421,"type":"genre","name":"Gothic Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":272,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":151519479822379,"type":"genre","nam